  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Differentiate the following using the quotient rule.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p20-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{x+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{1-x}{2\\sqrt{x}(x+1)^2}$",
          "worked": "The numerator has derivative $\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}$ and the denominator has derivative $1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y'&=\\frac{(x+1)\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}-\\sqrt{x}}{(x+1)^2}\\\\y'&=\\frac{x+1-2x}{2\\sqrt{x}(x+1)^2}\\\\y'&=\\frac{1-x}{2\\sqrt{x}(x+1)^2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\frac{x+2}{2x^2\\sqrt{x+1}}$",
          "worked": "The numerator has derivative $\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+1}}$ and the denominator has derivative $1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y'&=\\frac{x\\cdot\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+1}}-\\sqrt{x+1}}{x^2}\\\\y'&=\\frac{x-2(x+1)}{2x^2\\sqrt{x+1}}\\\\y'&=-\\frac{x+2}{2x^2\\sqrt{x+1}}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 31
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+1}}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{x+2}{2\\sqrt{(x+1)^3}}$",
          "worked": "The numerator has derivative $1$ and the denominator has derivative $\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+1}}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y'&=\\frac{\\sqrt{x+1}-x\\cdot\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+1}}}{x+1}\\\\y'&=\\frac{2(x+1)-x}{2(x+1)\\sqrt{x+1}}\\\\y'&=\\frac{x+2}{2\\sqrt{(x+1)^3}}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      }
    ]
  },
